# Wave W17-Q (Route 123): master turf — ordered-field green: a bright tended green laid in the Berry Master’s rows — darker row-lines run through it at field intervals with ripe berry flecks standing along them (design: calm speckled grass through berry fields under a mountain; the shipped flower beds stand byte-preserved as the fields’ heart and the ground converts around them). Route 123’s own ground — the only row-drawn ground in the fleet: split from Route 121’s wild patrolled turf by the rows themselves (planted vs patrolled) and from Route 117’s open field green by structure: these fields are kept in lines.
